/build/*
!/build/container/
!/build/container/**
/dist/
/target/
/book/book/

# The pinned nightly ICEs on a stale incremental cache, and drops its crash dump
# in the working directory rather than under target/. Five of them reached a
# commit before this pattern existed; they are a compiler artifact of one
# machine's build and belong in no tree.
/rustc-ice-*.txt

# Key material must never reach a commit, whatever path it is dropped at: the
# development signing keys under build/dev-keys, and any TLS-inspection CA or
# private key an operator points the build at. These are catch-all patterns
# rather than specific paths precisely because the paths are configurable.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.gpg
*-ca.crt
